From c57a349825ed93a8ac373519fb7da5319fb75335 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mitsuru Oshima <oshima@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 20:02:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [M144-LTS] Add aura::Window::GeWeakPtrAsWindow()

This CL moves the WeakPtrFactory from GestureConsumer to subclasses,
and define WeakPtr getter for Window type, so that we can use the
same factory instance for super class and base casses, but still
use WeakPtr<aura::Window> but not WeakPtr<ui::GestureConsumer>.

Background:
There are increasing report w.r.t. dangling ptr for a window that can
be destroyed during a method call. This is to simplify the code
to deal with such situation (e.g. using WindowTracker or observers).

The weak pointer factory should be the last element in the class
structure, and there is no clean way to cast base::WeakPtr<Super>
to base::WeakPtr<Sub>.

C++ doesn't support covariance for template, so we can't just
define base::WeakPtr<aura::Window> GetWeakPtr.

And replced WindowTracker that tracks single window with Weakptr.

Bug: None

(cherry picked from commit d81edbd51ba06e32b3ecb78a6016ba7ff42f41e1)

